    {
      "name": "a grouped logical value followed by a comparison is a scalar",
      "notes": "Parentheses in `where` group a predicate OR a scalar; a `)` followed by a comparison, arithmetic, `in`, a range, or `.` makes the group a scalar operand. `a || b` yields an operand (SEMANTICS §8), so `(a || b) == 5` compares that operand.",
      "query": "r exists { where (a || b) == 5 }",
      "expect": {
        "result": true
      },
      "roots": {
        "r": [
          {
            "a": 0,
            "b": 5
          }
        ]
      }
    },
